# The cooperative evaluator deadline must FAIL the compile, under both
# compilers, with the same diagnostic.
#
# Why this case exists: yo-self had no compile deadline at all. TS armed one in
# its test runner (`src/test-runner.ts:544`, 600 s) so a runaway comptime loop
# failed one file with a named error; the self-hosted runner had nothing, so a
# hang burned the whole CI job's budget with no indication of which file caused
# it. That gap became load-bearing at P2.5 Group E, when TS stops existing.
#
# Determinism: the deadline is checked every 16384 dispatches, so a fixture too
# small to reach that count would never check and the case would pass
# vacuously. It does not happen here — a budget of 1 ms trips during PRELUDE
# evaluation, long before this fixture's own body is reached, which is also why
# the fixture can stay trivial.
#
# stdout_keep_match: asserts THE failure, not just A failure — without it any
# compile error at all would satisfy rc=1.
stdout_keep_match=exceeded the configured time limit
timeout=120
